# realtime-backend/.env — optional local overrides. Copy to `.env` and edit.
#
# `python server.py` with NO .env at all is a working install. Everything here
# exists for experiments and for the one config that is not yet the default.
#
# config.py::_load_dotenv uses os.environ.setdefault, so a real environment
# variable always wins AND, within this file, the FIRST occurrence of a key wins.
# Appending a second `EXPERTS=` line does nothing — edit the key in place.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: LLM narration (Task F). Unset => /narrate returns 503 and the
# frontend uses its local template narrator, so the demo runs fully offline.
# NEVER commit a real key; .env is gitignored, this .env.example is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=groq/compound-mini


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Config A (DEFAULT — what you get with no .env): 3 experts, risk band from
# a plain average of the per-expert probabilities.
#   EXPERTS=wavlm,hybrid,ssl
#   FUSION_MODE=heuristic_avg
#   SINGLE_EXPERT=hybrid
# `ssl` needs fairseq, which has no Python 3.13 build — on such a box this
# default cannot load and you must pick Config C below.
# NOTE: `hybrid_nc` was removed from config.py; it is no longer a valid name.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Config B: the FIRST bandwidth-robust LFCC expert drives the band. Superseded by
# Config C below — keep this only to reproduce older numbers.
#
# hybrid_br_best.pth is local-only (not on the Hub) — it must already be in
# model_cache/ or the expert refuses to load. That alone makes Config C the
# better default for a fresh clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPERTS=wavlm,hybrid,hybrid_br
# FUSION_MODE=single
# SINGLE_EXPERT=hybrid_br
# CALIBRATOR_PATH=artifacts/calibrator_hybrid_br.json


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Config C (RECOMMENDED for a live demo): hybrid_maxbr drives the band.
#
# Like hybrid_br it applies the 7 kHz parity band gate, so its verdict does not
# depend on which resampler produced the audio (0.03 logit shift from
# out-of-band energy, vs 23.55 for `hybrid`). Unlike hybrid_br it is on the Hub
# (sarosh22/Final_LFCC), so this config works on a fresh clone with no manual
# file copying.
#
# It replaces hybrid_br because it is better at the SHIPPED policy bands on
# held-out generators:
#   hybrid_br     88.1% spoof caught @ 2.9% false alarm
#   hybrid_maxbr  91.5% spoof caught @ 1.7% false alarm
# One caveat: `optispeech` recall drops to 26.9% (hybrid_br had no generator
# below 50%). hybrid_br stays in EXPERTS as a side card for comparison.
#
# CALIBRATOR_PATH *must* be hybrid_maxbr's own artifact: FUSION_MODE=single reads
# the headline band through it, and server.py raises at startup if it belongs to
# another expert. Both gated calibrators declare band_gate_hz=7000, so the gate
# check cannot catch a swap between them — only this one can. Use an absolute
# path or one relative to realtime-backend/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPERTS=wavlm,hybrid,hybrid_br,hybrid_maxbr
# FUSION_MODE=single
# SINGLE_EXPERT=hybrid_maxbr
# CALIBRATOR_PATH=artifacts/calibrator_hybrid_maxbr.json


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rarely needed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEVICE=cpu
# PREFETCH_MODELS=1        # download every Hub checkpoint at startup
# WINDOW_SEC=4.0
# HOP_SEC=0.5
# EMA_ALPHA=0.3
